    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP today, the priority is capitalizing on high-ceiling matchups against soft pitching. **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 85.94 efficiency score, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Mikolas and a premium leadoff spot; his ability to exploit Mikolas\u2019s slow delivery makes him our primary weapon for closing the stolen base gap. **Gabriel Moreno** (70.65) and **Austin Riley** (70.38) also project as high-impact starts. **Austin Riley** is particularly well-positioned, as the park factors (+16%) and his favorable platoon split against Baz provide a massive floor despite the lower batting order position. Meanwhile, **Isaac Paredes** (68.21) and **James Wood** (67.80) are strong, high-floor plays, with **James Wood** specifically benefiting from an elite xwOBA that should translate well against Drake.\n\nWhile our core lineup is set, the bench decisions were tight. **Travis Bazzana** (39.05) just missed the cut, falling shy of our 40.0 floor due to a tough matchup against Rasmussen and negative park adjustments. Similarly, **Cole Young** (37.53) showed promise with a leadoff bump, but the reality of facing a dominant arm like deGrom\u2014who mandates a severe reduction in expectations for all hitters\u2014forced his exclusion. We are also monitoring the risk associated with **Jose Caballero** (51.08); while he provides necessary speed, his matchup against the elite Cristopher S\u00e1nchez is a volatility point, and we are still awaiting official confirmation of his #8 spot in the lineup. With **Giancarlo Stanton** and **Trevor Story** still on the IL, we are leaning heavily on the current depth of **Brice Turang** and **Mickey Moniak** to provide stable production. Owners should stay alert for late-breaking weather or lineup changes, particularly with **Jose Caballero**, as any further demotion in the order would likely render him a bench-only candidate for this specific slate.",
